# NexGuard L7 ZTNA CoreDNS configuration (ADR-012).
#
# Single forwarder model — the operator chooses ONE resolver to
# forward everything to via the `COREDNS_FORWARD_TO` env var:
#
#   * Use the company's internal DNS (e.g. 10.0.235.250) if the
#     same resolver handles both internal corporate names AND
#     forwards public queries upstream. Typical enterprise setup.
#     Trade-off: public lookups go through one extra hop.
#
#   * Use a public resolver (1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8) if VPN clients only
#     need public DNS plus the L7 app hostnames from the hosts
#     file. Fastest public lookups; non-L7 internal names won't
#     resolve.
#
# Declared L7 application hostnames are resolved by the `hosts`
# plugin (reads /etc/nexguard/internal-hosts, written by Phoenix's
# FzHttp.L7.CoreDnsHosts) BEFORE the forward — so L7 apps always
# resolve to their VIP regardless of which upstream is configured.
#
# Bind to all interfaces inside the shared nexguard net namespace
# so the wg-nexguard tunnel sees us (VPN clients send DNS queries
# to the gateway's WG-side IP).

. {
  hosts /etc/nexguard/internal-hosts {
    reload 1s
    ttl 30
    fallthrough
  }
  forward . {$COREDNS_FORWARD_TO} {
    max_concurrent 1000
    health_check 5s
  }
  cache 300
  errors
  log . "{remote}:{port} {>id} {type} {name} -> {rcode} {>rflags} {rsize} {duration}"
}
